    'STDF (Standard Test Data Format, SEMI/Teradyne) is the binary datalog produced by ATE testers during wafer sort and final test — it carries per-part results (PRR), bins, and per-measurement parametric records (PTR). KLARF (KLA Results File) is the ASCII output of defect inspection tools (KLA-Tencor and similar) — it carries defect coordinates, sizes, class numbers and cluster information per wafer. Test (STDF) tells you how die passed; inspection (KLARF) tells you what physical defects were seen.': 'STDF (Standard Test Data Format, SEMI/Teradyne) is the binary datalog produced by ATE testers during wafer sort and final test — it carries per-part results (PRR), bins, and per-measurement parametric records (PTR). KLARF (KLA Results File) is the ASCII output of defect inspection tools (KLA-Tencor and similar) — it carries defect coordinates, sizes, class numbers and cluster information per wafer. Test (STDF) tells you how die passed; inspection (KLARF) tells you what physical defects were seen.',
