    'KLARF 1.0/1.2 files are parsed as ASCII text: header tokens (LotID, WaferID, DeviceID, StepID, DiePitch), the DefectRecordSpec column schema, and the DefectList rows. Clustering is a DBSCAN-style spatial grouping that flags scratch (high aspect ratio) and hotspot (dense burst) patterns.': 'KLARF 1.0/1.2 files are parsed as ASCII text: header tokens (LotID, WaferID, DeviceID, StepID, DiePitch), the DefectRecordSpec column schema, and the DefectList rows. Clustering is a DBSCAN-style spatial grouping that flags scratch (high aspect ratio) and hotspot (dense burst) patterns.',
