    'PTR retention is capped to bound memory on very large datalogs: the background worker keeps up to 200,000 PTR records, while the automatic main-thread fallback (browsers without worker support) keeps 5,000. Files beyond the active cap show a partial parametric sample (bin/yield data from PRR is never capped).': 'PTR retention is capped to bound memory on very large datalogs: the background worker keeps up to 200,000 PTR records, while the automatic main-thread fallback (browsers without worker support) keeps 5,000. Files beyond the active cap show a partial parametric sample (bin/yield data from PRR is never capped).',
